    "title": "Is Publix open on Easter Sunday? Hours, if stores are open in Florida",
    "text": "April 3, 2026, 6:55 a.m. ETEaster is one of only three holidays Publix closes for, along with Thanksgiving and Christmas.Several other grocery stores, including Walmart and Whole Foods, will be open on Easter.Shoppers should verify the hours of their local stores as some may have reduced holiday hours.Today is Good Friday, just two days away from Easter Sunday, so you have time to do your holiday grocery shopping.But are you worried you'll forget a chocolate bunny for a basket, a hostess gift for Easter brunch, or an ingredient for your deviled eggs on Sunday?Many Florida shoppers opt for their beloved Publix for regular grocery shopping, but is it open on Easter? Here's what to know before you leave your home.When is Easter 2026?Easter Sunday is this weekend, on April 5.In 2025, Easter fell much later in the month, on April 20. This year, Eastern Orthodox Easter will fall on Sunday, April 12, 2026.The holiday's date is determined by the moon and is celebrated on the Sunday after the first full moon after the spring equinox, according to Christianity.com.Will Publix be open on Easter holiday 2026?No. Publix locations in Florida and other states will not be open on Easter Sunday, which is Sunday, April 5.Of all the holidays throughout the year, Publix stores are closed only three days: Thanksgiving, Christmas, and Easter. Will Publix liquor stores or pharmacies be open?No, Publix liquor stores and pharmacies will also be closed.What grocery stores are open on Easter Sunday 2026?While many stores close for Easter Sunday each year, a few will remain open across Florida:Whole FoodsSproutsWinn-DixieTrader Joe'sBJ's WholesaleWalmartShop with Walmart+ membershipNote that some of these retailers may have reduced hours at all or some of their locations due to the holiday. Check your nearest location's hours before you head to the store.Samantha Neely is a trending reporter for the USA TODAY NETWORK-Florida, covering pop culture, theme parks, breaking news and more. You can get all of Florida’s best content directly in your inbox each weekday by signing up for the free newsletter, Florida TODAY, at https://floridatoday.com/newsletters.Our editors independently choose our recommendations. Some content is produced with paid support from a third party, however our editorial decisions remain independent. If you buy through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices and availability may change.",
